"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/167137697?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frop-qart","html_url":"https://github.com/frop-qart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frop-qart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frop-qart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frop-qart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frop-qart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frop-qart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frop-qart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frop-qart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frop-qart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frop-qart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-16T20:31:58Z","updated_at":"2025-08-16T20:31:58Z","body":"I was able to reproduce this bug on my system as well on 4.4.1-stable and 4.5.beta. However, for me it's occurring even if the client sends a disconnect request which the server receives. It seems like the problem is [line 136 in enet_connection.cpp](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/modules/enet/enet_connection.cpp#L136). The `_on_disconnect()` method sets the peer to nullptr no matter what. I'm honestly a bit confused why it's here since the expected behavior is to pretty much always return the peer that was disconnected. I'd appreciate if anyone can explain the purpose of this method at this line.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3193892614/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]